{#
  « Rattacher à », answered by typing a place or a month.

  The control this replaces was a `<select>` holding the CROSS PRODUCT of
  every visible place and every stay it ever hosted — two hundred lines on
  a unit in its tenth year, in an order nobody can predict, to find the
  camp whose contract is on the screen. The same shape the finance module
  already uses for « quelle créance ? » and « quel mouvement ? »: type,
  wait a beat, ask the server, click a result.

  **The `<select>` is still here, and that is deliberate.** It is what the
  form submits when JavaScript does not run, and the script REMOVES it on
  upgrade so the two controls can never both post a `camp_id`. It no
  longer holds everything either: it holds the same ranked shortlist the
  search box opens on — the stay this message's own dates name first, then
  what is still to come — which is the answer far more often than not.

  Parameters:
    message_id     -- the message being attached; makes every id unique
    options        -- the shortlist, as partials/form_field.html.twig wants it
    preferred_ids  -- stays this message's dates name, best first
    searchable     -- false when no search service was built: the select
                      stays and no search box is offered
#}
<div class="stay-picker" data-stay-picker
     data-preferred="{{ preferred_ids|join(',') }}">
    <div data-stay-picker-fallback>
        {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
            field_id: 'camp-' ~ message_id,
            field_name: 'camp_id',
            label: 'Rattacher à',
            type: 'select', size: 'sm',
            options: options,
            wrapper_class: 'mb-0',
        } only %}
    </div>

    {% if searchable %}
        {# Hidden until the script takes over: a search box that cannot
           search is worse than a list. #}
        <div class="d-none" data-stay-picker-search>
            {% include 'partials/form_field.html.twig' with {
                field_id: 'camp-search-' ~ message_id,
                label: 'Rattacher à',
                size: 'sm',
                wrapper_class: 'mb-0',
                placeholder: 'Lieu, mois, année…',
                autocomplete: 'off',
            } only %}

            {# What the form actually posts. Disabled so it stays out of
               the request until the script has enabled it — until then the
               `<select>` above is the one control that answers. #}
            <input type="hidden" name="camp_id" value="" disabled data-stay-picker-value>

            <div class="stay-picker__results list-group d-none" data-stay-picker-results
                 role="listbox" aria-label="Séjours proposés"></div>
        </div>
    {% endif %}
</div>
